# Motion preview convention

- Every preview, in both preset cards and the detail panel, must use skeleton shapes.
- Represent titles and descriptions with rounded bars, images with neutral blocks, and icons with simple geometric placeholders.
- Do not put sample copy, photos, illustrations, emoji or decorative symbols inside preview scenes. For example, a button contains a short pale bar, never “Continue”.
- Semantic status icons are allowed when the motion demonstrates that state (for example, a completion check after progress finishes). Keep labels as skeleton bars.
- Preserve each scene’s recognizable structure: content has an image and sections; navigation has a sidebar and richer modal fields; buttons retain their surface and shadow.
- Animate the intended elements using the shared runtime config. Do not add shimmer to static skeleton placeholders unless the preset specifically demonstrates shimmer.
- Keep real preset names, filter labels, control labels, prompts and accessible names outside the scene readable.
- Hover Lift belongs to Card only, not Button.
- Keep default motion duration at 400ms unless the user explicitly changes it.

- Card controls expose semantic parameters only (spread, depth, direction, threshold, scale, timing). Preview and generated prompt derive from one resolved runtime config; never export sampled preview transforms as implementation instructions.

- Keep preview heights identical across presets within the grid, and identical across presets in the detail panel. Clip oversized scenes inside the shared bounds; never enlarge one preset’s preview. Stack Fan Swipe uses tall cards with their lower tails clipped.
